    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hidden within the exclusive Mariners Cove development in the heart of Howth, Coleridge is an attractive detached family residence occupying a generous, private site with fine sized gardens and a cobblelock driveway with ample parking. This is a modern home with a split level interior and flexibility, offering c. 2,140 square feet of bright, well-proportioned accommodation that will appeal to growing families, those seeking multi-generational living or buyers looking for a home with adaptable spaces to suit changing needs.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation has been thoughtfully arranged creating a practical balance between spacious reception rooms and generous bedroom accommodation. The welcoming entrance hall forms the centrepiece of the home and immediately conveys the sense of space throughout. There are five well-proportioned bedrooms, including the principal bedroom with en-suite, together with a large family bathroom, guest WC and utility room. The versatile layout allows some space to be easily adapted for working from home depending on requirements, while the internal courtyard introduces natural light into the centre of the house and creates a unique architectural feature.\r\n\r\nThe main living accommodation enjoys an elevated setting overlooking the surrounding garden. The main living room features tall windows and a stove, adjacent is a second reception room with a curved bay window, creating an ideal space for entertaining. The spacious kitchen/breakfast room provides an excellent everyday family hub with ample room for dining and direct access to the garden.\r\n\r\nOutside, the garden provides a wonderful sense of privacy, with mature boundaries and generous outdoor space surrounding the property. The extensive driveway comfortably accommodates numerous vehicles while the elevated position further enhances the feeling of space and seclusion.\r\nMariners Cove is one of Howth's most established and sought-after residential developments, renowned for its peaceful setting while remaining just minutes from the vibrant village centre. Residents enjoy immediate access to an outstanding range of amenities including the picturesque harbour, renowned seafood restaurants, cafés, boutique shops and scenic cliff walks. Howth DART Station provides regular services to the city centre, while excellent schools, yacht clubs, golf courses, beaches and coastal walks are all within easy reach. Dublin Airport, the M50 and M1 motorway network are also readily accessible.\r\n\r\nViewing is available by appointment with Conor & Rory Gallagher Tel: 01-8183000 info@gallagherquigley.ie"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 8.36m x 7.53m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.35m x 5.34m \r\n\r\n\r\nEn-suite - 1.51m x 3.35m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 4.49m x 3.35m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.35m x 3.36m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 - 3.33m x 2.95m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 5 - 3.33m x 2.67m \r\n\r\n\r\nWC - \r\n\r\n\r\nUtility Room - 2.38m x 1.71m \r\n\r\n\r\nLanding - 4.8m x 2.56m \r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 5.33m x 4.43m \r\n\r\n\r\nDinign Room - 4.8m x 4.54m \r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room - 4.56m x 4.43m \r\n\r\n\r\n"
      },
